# Project rules

## Exception: OPS-REPO-P02 (file layout)

Docker and deployment files are not kept in the standard locations
(`docker/<service>/`, Compose files in the repository root) but in these
directories:

- `legacy/app/docker/**`
- `legacy/app/docker-compose*.yml`
- `legacy/tools/deploy/**`

Reason: inherited repository structure; the move to the standard layout is
planned separately.

The common `infra` rules and the rules of the DevOps profiles chosen in
`.dev-standard/config.json` apply to these paths.

## Exception: OPS-PIPE-P07 (Git release model)

This repository follows neither the branch-based nor the tag-based release
model: production is deployed only by a manual run of `Ops: Deploy` with an
image tag that was built from `main`.

Reason: inherited release process; the move to the tag-based model is planned
separately.

`.dev-standard/config.json` therefore lists no release model (`flow-branch`,
`flow-tag`). The deployment documentation describes how a release reaches
each environment. The common `infra` rules and the chosen deployment method
still apply.
